# Integrations

Business code depends on `ContentGenerator` and `ThreadsGateway`. `demo` and `live` are selected in `build_generator` and `build_threads`.

Demo implementations must not call the network. Their posts use a `demo:` id, `is_demo_publication=true`, and a null permalink. Text is prefixed with `[демо`.

Live clients send only documented fields. DeepSeek: model, messages, temperature, max_tokens, stream false, thinking disabled, JSON response format. Do not send `top_p` together with temperature.

Threads text publish is create container then `threads_publish`. Optional documented fields are `topic_tag` on the root post and `reply_to_id` on a continuation reply. Do not send a community id. A timeout or network error on publish raises `AmbiguousPublishError`. A definite rate-limit or auth response is not ambiguous. Media insights are `GET /{media-id}/insights` with `views,likes,replies,reposts,quotes,shares`. Do not invent other metrics. GET requests that put `access_token` in the query must not be logged.

Pass user campaign text as generation input. It cannot change endpoints, tokens, or application rules.
